## What this restores

This PR turns the current docs/core-only repository into a runnable Mura desktop baseline without discarding the newer 1.0 platform-core work already on `main`.

- sandboxed Electron shell with transparent always-on-top companion window;
- `window.mura` preload bridge with context isolation and no raw IPC exposure;
- 16-sector cursor attention + continuous rig response contract;
- procedural blink and bounded autonomous behavior;
- local memory, relationship/episode/rare-event primitives;
- permission ledger and local object-intelligence utilities;
- timers, surface graph/physics primitives;
- minimal first-party Mura Character Pack;
- drag/drop file handoff baseline;
- Electron Builder package targets and runtime-contract tests.

## Deliberate limits

This is a **smoke-testable integration baseline**, not a claim that every 0.5–0.9 feature documented in the repository has already been re-imported. The full historical Home UI, native window adapter, rich Mura animation library, continuity/replica/pairing/live-visit implementation and historical test suite still need to be restored or re-integrated.

The current minimal Character Pack intentionally maps multiple actions to the same canonical fallback image until the richer art bundle is imported.

## Validation performed locally

- clean alpha runtime/core subset: **12/12 tests passed**;
- JS syntax checks passed;
- character pack validation passed in the combined source workspace;
- separately, the reconstructed 0.5 + current 1.0-core workspace passed **64/64 tests**.

The Electron GUI itself still needs a real macOS/Windows smoke test, especially transparent-window behavior, global shortcuts, drag/drop from Finder/Explorer and multi-monitor positioning.

## Product step

This PR moves Mura beyond a floating overlay: Mura can opt into **window geometry as a physical surface**, attach to a real application window, and follow it when that host window moves.

### Added
- macOS geometry adapter via System Events;
- Windows geometry adapter via Win32 enumeration from PowerShell;
- Linux adapter via `wmctrl`;
- window titles are deliberately discarded;
- geometry sampling is disabled by default and stored as an explicit local preference;
- Surface Graph integration in the runnable Electron shell;
- attach to nearest usable top edge;
- follow an attached window as geometry changes;
- leave-surface action returning Mura to the desktop floor;
- tray controls for geometry permission / perch / leave;
- narrow preload APIs for surface actions;
- runtime capabilities now report the opt-in geometry adapter;
- alpha version moves to `1.0.0-alpha.3`.

## Privacy boundary

This does not add screenshots, OCR, microphone access or content inspection. The surface adapter collects geometry and an app/process owner identifier only; window titles are not retained. Geometry remains off until the user enables it.

## Validation

Local alpha.3 suite: **23/23 tests passed** plus syntax checks.

New tests cover macOS/Windows/Linux geometry parsers, disabled-by-default behavior, macOS permission failure detection, Surface Graph landing constraints and the renderer/main IPC boundary.

## Known limits

- real macOS/Windows permission behavior still needs an acceptance test;
- Linux requires `wmctrl` for now;
- attachment currently moves the companion window directly rather than playing a run/jump/landing transition;
- richer Mura art and Home UI are the next user-facing restoration step.

Alpha 4 reconciles the richer character-presence work into the current Mura 1.0 runtime.

Included:
- `1.0.0-alpha.4` runtime entrypoint;
- restored Mura attention, idle, wave, jump, directional run and pose assets;
- Alpha 4 desktop renderer and compatibility layered rig;
- Home UI;
- Focus / Quiet / timers;
- relationship, episode and rare-event runtime wiring;
- explicit consent handoff flow (`inspect -> remember/open/reveal`), replacing automatic persistence on drop;
- Share Card flow;
- run/jump/landing window locomotion on top of the opt-in Surface Engine;
- `Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+H` Home shortcut;
- Character Pack validation in CI;
- reconciled runtime-contract tests;
- README / roadmap / Alpha 4 implementation docs reconciled with actual source;
- stale `UPLOAD_PLAN.tmp` removed.

Validation required before merge:
- `npm test`;
- `npm run check`;
- `npm run validate:character`.

Post-merge acceptance work:
- real macOS/Windows smoke test for transparent windows, OS geometry permissions, global shortcuts, Finder/Explorer drag-and-drop and multi-monitor positioning.

This PR no longer claims historical 0.5–0.9 modules are all wired into the current runtime.
